# Trivy misconfiguration suppressions for this repo.
# Each entry is intentional and documented; revisit if the module changes.

# AVD-AWS-0132 — S3 bucket not encrypted with a customer-managed KMS key.
# The service provisions buckets with default SSE; customer-managed KMS keys are
# left to the consumer to layer on when required (flexible by design).
AVD-AWS-0132

# AVD-AWS-0345 — IAM policy allows 's3:*' action.
#   dynamodb/specs/requirements/aws/main.tf, statement "ManageStateBuckets"
#
# The role manages one state bucket per service instance, and the scripts use six
# operations on them — head-bucket, create-bucket, put-bucket-versioning,
# delete-bucket, delete-objects and list-object-versions — plus the reads and
# writes the tofu backend performs on the state object. s3:* is wider than that.
#
# The resource is already scoped to arn:aws:s3:::np-service-*, so the finding is
# about the action rather than the target. It is still worth fixing: s3:* covers
# PutBucketPolicy and PutBucketPublicAccessBlock, and each link's access key sits
# in that state in clear text, so a compromised role could publish the bucket.
#
# Accepted until the actions are enumerated in two statements, one for the bucket
# and one for its objects. The expiry makes this check fail again if nobody did.
AVD-AWS-0345 exp:2026-10-31
